<title>NEW ZEALAND: Hellaby buys back 9 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Hellaby buys back 9 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment company Hellaby Holdings said on Monday acceptances for its 1:5 pro rata share buyback offer totalled nine million shares, or NZ$16.7 million.</p>
<p>The offer was for a maximum of 11.9 million shares at $1.85 per share.</p>
<p>All applications were fully satisfied.</p>
<p>The acceptances included seven million shares from substantial security holdings.  </p>
<p>The number of Hellaby shares on issue will reduce to 50.3 million from 59.3 million, with Green &amp; McCahill Group holding 15 million, Managing Director Tur Borren's family trust four million and Anteon Investments one million.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
</text>
